    <!-- START: Steps Block -->
    <!-- The arrow came from the retired "Steps Block (w/ arrow heading)" when
         the two merged (user decision 2026-08-21). data-display-toggle makes
         it optional: it is the SOLE member of its column once the light/dark
         twins fold into one, and a sole member earns no Display Select
         otherwise. The flag goes on the FIRST twin — mergeSwapPairs folds the
         second in before flags are read, so a flag on the dark image is inert.
         NOTE: hiding the arrow does NOT widen the heading. The 90px column
         stays, per the 2026-08-20 decision that hidden content leaves columns
         at their authored widths; making the row collapse needs a Display
         option that rewrites the whole arrangement, which the generator does
         not do today. -->
    <!-- data-mobile-only-padding-right was here until 2026-08-22. The 120px
         arrow column does pin the desktop layout, so with the arrow SHOWN the
         right gutter moves nothing at 600px (measured 2026-08-21 — glyphs
         identical across 0/8/16/32). But the "No Arrow" arrangement below
         collapses the row to one full-width column, and there the gutter is
         live at desktop: copy box 64..600 at 0px versus 64..536 at 64px
         (measured 2026-08-22 on the identical Icon Row shape). An arrangement
         Select is editor-owned exactly as copy is, so this is the same call
         the 2026-08-21 decision made about copy-dependent inertness — the
         first editor who picks "No Arrow" brings the control alive under a
         label that says "Mobile". Every row that offers an alternate lost the
         flag together: Icon Row, Podcast Episode Block, the three Feedback
         Poll answers and this one. Podcast Streaming Block and Signature Card
         (photo) keep theirs — they have no alternate, so nothing can unpin
         them. -->
    <mj-section css-class="text-block block" background-color="#F5FAF1" padding="16px 64px">
      <mj-group>
        <mj-column width="120px" vertical-align="top" css-class="step-icon">
          <mj-image src="assets/icon-arrow-orange.png" alt="" width="70px" align="left" padding="0 16px 0 0" css-class="light-only" />
          <mj-raw><!--[if !mso]><!--></mj-raw>
          <mj-image src="assets/icon-arrow-orange.png" alt="" width="70px" align="left" padding="0 16px 0 0" css-class="dark-only" data-style-dark-mode />
          <mj-raw><!--<![endif]--></mj-raw>
        </mj-column>
        <mj-column width="352px" vertical-align="middle" css-class="step-text">
          <mj-text padding="0">
            <h3 style="color:#39B54A;font-style:italic;">It's easy to send your comment&mdash;<br />just follow these simple steps:</h3>
          </mj-text>
        </mj-column>
      </mj-group>
    </mj-section>
    <!-- The section below is this row's ALTERNATE ARRANGEMENT: same content,
         no image, one full-width column. data-alt-arrangement folds it into
         the row's own Select as a third option instead of rendering it, so an
         editor picks Left / Right / No Arrow from one control. It has to be
         AUTHORED rather than generated: the collapsed column needs
         mj-column-per-100 AND its head rules, and column widths are never
         generated. Keep its copy byte-identical to the primary's — the pairing
         matches on value, and drift does NOT fail loudly: measured 2026-08-22,
         one changed letter unpairs the alternate, which then renders as its
         OWN band (the content twice) and renumbers every band after it, with
         only an INFO note from the importer. The loud signal is check-catalog's
         alternate-arrangement guard, which compares the two copies here. -->
    <mj-section data-alt-arrangement="No Arrow" css-class="text-block block" background-color="#F5FAF1" padding="16px 64px">
      <mj-column>
        <mj-text padding="0">
          <h3 style="color:#39B54A;font-style:italic;">It's easy to send your comment&mdash;<br />just follow these simple steps:</h3>
        </mj-text>
      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>
    <mj-section css-class="text-block block" background-color="#F5FAF1" padding="0 64px 16px">
      <mj-column>
        <mj-text padding="0 0 16px">
          <p style="font-size:16px;margin-bottom:2px;"><span class="step-num">&nbsp;1&nbsp;</span>&nbsp; <b>Share your name.</b></p>
          <p style="font-size:16px;margin-top:0;">Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet, consectetur adipiscing elit sed do eiusmod tempor incididunt ut labore et dolore magna aliqua.</p>
          <p style="font-size:16px;margin-bottom:2px;"><span class="step-num">&nbsp;2&nbsp;</span>&nbsp; <b>Thank [Agency Name].</b></p>
          <p style="font-size:16px;margin-top:0;">Let them know you appreciate the chance to weigh in.</p>
          <p style="font-size:16px;margin-bottom:2px;"><span class="step-num">&nbsp;3&nbsp;</span>&nbsp; <b>Say why this matters to you.</b></p>
          <p style="font-size:16px;margin-top:0;">Explain why it's essential that park interpretation reflects all of America's history&mdash;and why strong staffing and funding are needed to make that possible.</p>
          <p style="font-size:16px;margin-bottom:2px;"><span class="step-num">&nbsp;4&nbsp;</span>&nbsp; <b>Add your personal touch.</b></p>
          <p style="font-size:16px;margin-top:0;">Share a meaningful park memory or experience&mdash;something that helped you learn or feel connected.</p>
          <p style="font-size:16px;margin-bottom:2px;"><span class="step-num">&nbsp;5&nbsp;</span>&nbsp; <b>Close with your request.</b></p>
          <p style="font-size:16px;margin-top:0;">Call on the NPS to research, preserve, and share all aspects of our history&mdash;and to fund this work so these stories can be told.</p>
        </mj-text>
        <mj-button width="auto"
          href="https://tpl.org"
          align="left" padding="0 0 16px" color="#ffffff" background-color="#006837">LEARN MORE</mj-button>
        <mj-text css-class="wysiwyg link-accent" padding="0">
          <p style="font-size:13px;line-height:19px;font-style:italic;">This button will take you to <a href="https://tpl.org">[the public comment portal]</a>, the official site where you can send your comment straight to [Agency Name].</p>
        </mj-text>
      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>
    <mj-section css-class="spacer-block block" padding="0">
      <mj-column>
        <mj-spacer height="16px" />
      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>
    <!-- END: Steps Block -->

