         only an INFO note from the importer. The loud signal is check-catalog's
         alternate-arrangement guard, which compares the two copies here.
         All three answer rows carry one. They stay INDEPENDENT controls, so
         hiding is per-answer — which is what lets a poll keep one emphasis
         icon if that is the intent, at the cost of letting an editor build a
         ragged list. Matches Icon Row, Steps Block and Podcast Episode Block,
         the three rows of identical shape. -->
    <mj-section data-alt-arrangement="No Icon" css-class="poll-block block" background-color="#ffffff" padding="0 64px 8px">
      <mj-column>
        <mj-text padding="0">
          <p style="font-size:16px;"><a href="https://tpl.org"><strong>Very important</strong></a></p>
        </mj-text>
      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>
